# Response headers for the static files (Workers Static Assets reads this file from dist/; it is
# not served itself). The API routes (/api, /ws, /room, /lobby, /nodes) run the Worker and are
# unaffected. Every page is served from here: index.html (/, /tv and any other path: the SPA
# fallback) and replay.html (the replay viewer, /replay.html), so this one rule covers them all.
#
# Content-Security-Policy, checked against the code by tests/csp.test.mjs:
#   script-src   the build's own modules (the music's AudioWorklet too), 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the
#                physics wasm, the sha256 of each page's inline scripts (today only index.html's /tv/
#                redirect; the test fails when one changes without its hash), Turnstile, and Cloudflare Web
#                Analytics' beacon, which the zone injects (it reports to /cdn-cgi/rum: 'self').
#   style-src    'unsafe-inline': the icon sprite and the debug overlays set style attributes.
#   connect-src  the API and the match, room and lobby sockets ('self'), and the community nodes:
#                wss:// hosts on any domain.
#   frame-src    the Turnstile challenge. frame-ancestors 'none': never in a frame (X-Frame-Options too).
# Strict-Transport-Security: HTTPS only, for a year, subdomains included (sp1 serves only HTTPS).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-OLpvSajAB4kwvloMmj2FyovlRe1qITBh8oF1/nh19cA=' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' wss:; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# No long-lived Cache-Control on /assets/* although Vite content-hashes them: a request for a missing
# asset (an old tab during a deploy) gets the SPA fallback index.html, and _headers rules match the
# path, so that HTML would be cached as immutable. ETag revalidation (304) stays cheap.
